jq import: $(jq.import name,text) makes the store namespace name as create makes it,
handles and star twins included, and loads the one JSON text as its value, so jq joins
the engines that take import. Its star form takes a variable's name and its dedented
value, so an at line above a define gives that define's name a store. Importing a name
again keeps the namespace and replaces its value. A star call whose argument names no
variable, a call with no text, and a text that does not load are fatal, and so is an
import from a forwarder, since a load's text does not travel the call channel. import is
not one of the store's operations, so main and the handles are unchanged. The sequence
of reading a backing, running the operation, and writing a backing back is one routine,
shared by the namespace call, the call channel and the import, and each engine builtin
joins the table through one routine.

